<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">
  <Sdk Name="Microsoft.Build.CentralPackageVersions" Version="2.0.1" />
  <Import Project="$(CommonFilesPath)RuntimeComponentPreamble.csproj" />

  <!--
    This project builds to assembly identity 'ConditionalControls' (taken from the project name).
    The sibling project Features\Conditionals\ConditionalsModel overrides its AssemblyName to that
    *same* identity - see the note there for why. Nothing references both, so nothing mis-resolves,
    but two files named ConditionalControls.winmd exist under BuildOutput and it is easy to inspect
    the wrong one.

    Nothing has a ProjectReference to this project, so a reference search alone makes it look unused.
    It is not: it is a codegen baseline target. See Tests\UnitTests\CodegenTargets.txt and
    CodegenTests.Codegen_ConditionalControls, with masters under
    TestMasters\RegressionProjects\Features\Conditionals\ConditionalControls. Its XamlTypeInfo.g.cs
    baseline differs from ConditionalsModel's, so the two cover different generated output.
  -->

</Project>